<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore Oct industrial output up 1.8 pct on year.</title>
<headline>Singapore Oct industrial output up 1.8 pct on year.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's total manufacturing output in October grew by 1.8 percent compared to the same month of the previous year, after falling 6.7 per cent in September, the Economic Development Board (EDB) said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>The EDB said in a statement cumulative growth for manufacturing in the first 10 months of 1996 was 4.5 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>Table of Singapore's top 10 industries:</p>
<p>				    (pct change over previous year)</p>
<p>				     Oct 96	 Sep 96	 Aug 96</p>
<p>   *Total manufacturing	 1.8	   -6.7	   -7.0</p>
<p>    Electronics		   4.2	   -7.1	   -4.4</p>
<p>    Fabricated Metals	  -4.0	   -8.4	   -7.4</p>
<p>    Transport Equipment	 0.1	  -18.9	  -18.2</p>
<p>    Machinery x-electronics  -8.7	   -8.5	   -7.3</p>
<p>    Petroleum products	 -2.8	   14.8	   -3.8</p>
<p>    Paints, pharmaceuticals -11.0	  -11.3	  -24.5</p>
<p>    Printing/publishing	-1.2	   -7.9	   -3.3</p>
<p>    Industrial chems/gas     92.7	   -3.0	   -0.8</p>
<p>    Electrical machines	 9.2	    0.6	   -0.8</p>
<p>    Plastic products	   -6.5	  -14.7	  -17.6</p>
<p>* Total manufacturing output excludes rubber processing.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
